            in the bid queue for            W - Withdraw Outstanding Order(s)
            later acceptance by some        D - Display Options
            other trader.  The price        X - Exit to Market Menu
            for Purchases is                M - Market Selection
            determined by the current       Q - Quit Trader Program
            low price in the ask
            queue as displayed in the
            market window.  Upon selection of the "P" option, you will be
            prompted to supply the name of the desired contract and the maximum
            number that you are willing to buy at the current price.  (The
            current price will appear in the menu window for your information
            but it may not be changed.)  The highlighted contract in the market
            window will appear as the default contract -- it can be changed by
            using the Item Selection Keys or by typing the code of the desired
            contract.  Then press the "Enter" key to  move to the quantity
            entry, replace the default of 1 by typing in the desired value, and
            press "Enter" to move to the "Execute order" entry.  Repeatedly
            pressing the "Enter" key will rotate you through the entries for
            further editing.  (Note that you may cancel the order and return to
            the TRADING MENU by pressing the cancel (Esc) key or by positioning
            the cursor on the "Execute order" entry and typing "C".  When all
            entries appear as desired, position the cursor on the "Execute
            order" entry and press "Y" and then the "Enter" key.  At this point
            a message acknowledging the order will flash in the information
            window, you will be returned to the TRADING MENU, and the result of
            the transaction will appear in the market window after a short
            delay.

            There are also two "special" contracts, or rather contract
            bundles, which you can purchase in each market using the
            Purchase option.  The first is a "unit portfolio" which consists
            of one contract of each party listed in the current market, and
            it can be purchased at any time at the price of $1.00.  Note
            that unit portfolios are issued by the market system; this is
            the means by which new units of the contracts are placed in
            circulation.  To purchase one or more unit portfolios, select
            option P from the TRADING MENU, override the default contract by
            typing the unit portfolio code name "1$", and press "Enter". 
            The price of this unit portfolio will be set to one dollar and
            you can then indicate the number of unit portfolios you wish to
            purchase and execute the transaction.  

            The second "special" contract is a "market bundle".  Each market
            bundle, identified by the code name "MKT", generally consists of
            one contract of each party listed in the current market, and the
            purchase price of the bundle is determined as the sum of the ask
            prices on those contracts.  Market bundles are purchased on the
            market from other traders.  If one or more contracts in the
            market have no posted ask prices (that is if no trader has an
            outstanding order to sell), then those contracts will be omitted
            from the market bundle.  To purchase one or more market bundles,
            select P from the TRADING MENU, override the default contract
            name with the market bundle code name, "MKT", and press "Enter". 
            The sum of all posted ask prices will then be computed and that
            amount will appear as the price of the market bundle.  You may
            then proceed to indicate the number of market bundles you wish
            to purchase and to execute the transaction.  Note that the
            system will not permit you to purchase a market bundle if the
            posted ask price on any of the listed contracts is from an order
            submitted by you.  Note too that if the number of market bundles
            you request exceeds the number available at the computed price,
            your order will be only partially filled.

            When purchasing an individual contract or the "market bundle,"
            MKT, the price that appears in the window is the price at the
            time you selected the contract.  If you delay, it is indeed
            possible that the price may change due to another trader's
            action.  If you then attempt to make a purchase and the price
            has changed, the purchase will be executed only if the price of
            the selected contract has not increased.  If the price has
            increased, you will have to make a decision about whether you
            are willing to purchase the contract at the higher price.

      S - Sell at Current Bid$  --  This option provides a somewhat quicker
            facility for executing contract sales than through submission of
            an ask.  It will not, however, leave an order in the ask queue
            for later acceptance by some other trader.  The price for sales
            is determined by the current high price in the bid queue as
            displayed in the market window.  Upon selection of the "S"
            option, you will be prompted to supply the name of the desired
            contract and the maximum number that you are willing to sell at
            the current price.  (The current price will appear in the menu
            window for your information but it may not be changed.)  The
            highlighted contract in the market window will appear as the
            default contract -- it can be changed by using the Item
            Selection Keys or by typing the code of the desired contract. 
            Then press the "Enter" key to move to the quantity entry,
            replace the default of 1 by typing in the desired value, and
            press "Enter" to move to the "Execute order" entry.  Repeatedly
            pressing the "Enter" key will rotate you through the entries for
            further editing.  (Note that you may cancel the order and return
            to the TRADING MENU by pressing the cancel (Esc) key or by
            positioning the cursor on the "Execute order" entry and typing
            "C".)  When all entries appear as desired, position the cursor
            on the "Execute order" entry and press "Y" and then the "Enter"
            key.  At this point a message acknowledging the order will flash
            in the information window, you will be returned to the TRADING
            MENU, and the result of the transaction will appear in the
            market window after a short delay.

            There are also two "special" contracts, or rather contract
            bundles, which you can sell in each market using the Sell
            option.  The first is a "unit portfolio" which consists of one
            unit of each contract listed in the current market, and it can
            be sold at any time at the price of $1.00.  Note that unit
            portfolios are sold to (redeemed by) the market system; this is
            the means by which units of the contracts are removed from
            circulation.  To sell one or more unit portfolios, select option
            S from the TRADING MENU, override the default contract by typing
            the unit portfolio code name "1$", and press "Enter".  The price
            of this unit portfolio will be set to one dollar and you can
            then indicate the number of unit portfolios you wish to sell and
            execute the transaction.  

            The second "special" contract is a "market bundle".  Each market
            bundle, identified by the code name "MKT", generally consists of
            one contract of each party listed in the current market, and the
            sales price of the bundle is determined as the sum of the bid
            prices on those contracts.  Market bundles are sold on the
            market to other traders.  If one or more contracts in the market
            have no posted bid prices (that is if no trader has an
            outstanding order to buy), then those contracts will be omitted
            from the market bundle.  To sell one or more market bundles,
            select S from the TRADING MENU, override the default contract
            name with the market bundle code name, "MKT", and press "Enter". 
            The sum of all posted bid prices will then be computed and that
            amount will appear as the price of the market bundle.  You may
            then proceed to indicate the number of market bundles you wish
            to sell and to execute the transaction.  Note that the system
            will not permit you to sell a market bundle if the posted bid
            price on any of the listed contracts is from an order submitted
            by you.  Likewise the system will not accept an order to sell
            market bundles unless your contract holdings are sufficient to
            complete all of the bundles in your order.  Finally, if the
            number of market bundles in your order exceeds the number that
            can be sold at the computed price, your order will be only
            partially filled.

            When selling an individual contract or the "market bundle", MKT,
            the price that appears in the window is the price at the time
            you selected the contract.  If you delay, it is possible that
            the price may change due to another trader's action.  If you
            then attempt to make a sale and the price has changed, the sale
            will be executed only if the price of the selected contract has
            not decreased.  If the price has fallen, you will have to make
            a decision about whether you are willing to sell the contract at
            the lower price.

