~  MARKET DOWN TIMES AND RESPONSE DELAYS

      The market is designed to run continuously, but there are times when
it must pause to do backups and system maintenance, and there are times
when the Network on which the market operates is down for backups
initiated by the Faculty of Commerce and Business Administration Computer
Services Office.  

      The market operates as one continuously running program which receives
and processes requests from individual traders.  With many traders on the
system at one time, and particularly when there are many non-UBC-ESM users
on the network, there will be occasions when the master program or the
network server cannot keep pace with the flow of requests.  When it
happens that a particular request cannot be processed, a message will
appear on the screen describing the situation and the trader will be
advised to resubmit the request.

      There is a hardware-determined limit on the number of users that can
be connected to the market from remote sites at any one time.  When that
limit is approached, all users at both local and remote sites will be
notified of the problem and be given a few minutes to complete their
transactions and log out.  After that time interval, users will be logged
off by the system one at a time, beginning with the users who have been on
the system the longest, until the limit is no longer threatened.  


~  MISCELLANEOUS USAGE NOTES

      The system will prevent you from being logged into your account from
two or more locations (terminals) simultaneously.  An attempt to login
from a second location will cause an automatic logout at the previous
location.

      System activity will be slowed down by unattended terminals or by
improper termination of terminal sessions (eg., turning your PC off in the
middle of a market session).  Please follow the normal logout procedure --
selection of the X - Exit option from the each menu including the LOGIN
MENU -- as soon as your intended market activities are completed. 
Excessive neglect of this request may necessitate time limits on terminal
sessions and automatic logouts by the system.

      Your trading account is intended for the exclusive purposes of
executing orders for contract transactions and obtaining information about
market activity and your account status.  The system will prevent you from
accessing the Faculty of Commerce and Business Administration network in
any way except through the facilities of the market program.  That market
program is executed automatically upon login, and an automatic system
logout is performed upon termination of the program (selection of the X -
Exit option from the LOGIN MENU).  Any evidence of attempts to bypass this
system and gain direct access to the network for any reason will result in
revocation of your rights to trade on the UBC Election Stock Market.

