(6)  Outstanding orders are checked for expiration once each day just after
     midnight.  Thus, an order with a time of one day would expire at midnight
     on the day the order was submitted.

(7)  Only contracts with listed ask prices will be included in the MKT
     portfolio, and the system will sell only the number of MKT portfolios
     that it has available at the current ask prices.  These points are
     illustrated in the next example.

(8)  Analogous to the case discussed above related to Purchase at Market Price
     of the MKT portfolio, sales of MKT involve the transfer of contracts only
     if those contracts have current bid prices.  Also, the system will only
     let a trader sell the number of MKT portfolios that can be sold at current
     bid prices.  For example, suppose a trader wants to sell 25 MKT portfolios
     when only PC and BQ have outstanding bids on the system.  If at current
     bid prices there are 25 PC and 25 BQ contracts available, then the trader
     will be able to sell all 25 MKT portfolios.  However, if there are only
     15 BQ contracts wanted at the current bid price, the trade will be able
